1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:27,151
Most automated tests commit to one familiar order. RaceProof explores the other bounded timelines a TypeScript system can reach.

2
00:00:27,151 --> 00:00:52,687
Duplicate Payment: a timeout and retry can charge the same order twice. RaceProof finds the invariant failure.

3
00:00:52,687 --> 00:01:12,438
Every failure is a minimized, replayable counterexample with actors, transitions, immutable state snapshots, diffs, and invariant status.

4
00:01:12,438 --> 00:01:30,085
Turn the exact schedule into a self-contained Vitest regression.

5
00:01:30,085 --> 00:01:49,431
The fixed payment model uses idempotency. "No violation found within selected bounds" is a bounded result, not an unbounded proof.

6
00:01:49,431 --> 00:02:10,247
Inventory overselling and out-of-order chat are included as trusted buggy and fixed local examples.

7
00:02:10,247 --> 00:02:33,173
GPT-5.6 and Codex were used to build and review RaceProof. RaceProof has no AI runtime.

8
00:02:33,173 --> 00:02:36,173
RaceProof: explore the timelines your tests never run.
